# 05-multimodel — the point of model classes: route each phase of the work to the model that fits it.
# A big model writes the scaffold (the hard part: structure, the right todo!() seams), a small fast model
# fills each hole (cheap, parallel-ish, KV-shares the skeleton prefix), then the compile oracle grades the
# assembled result — no model needed for that, just rustc.
#
#   logscope-cli \
#     --model big=~/models/qwen2.5-coder-7b-instruct-q4_k_m.gguf \
#     --model small=~/.local/share/logscope/llama-3.2-1b-instruct-q4_k_m.gguf \
#     --max 1024 examples/05-multimodel.logscope
#
# Each :use switch is a full prefill on the newly-active model (it hasn't seen the lineage) — expected; the
# reuse you measured in 06 happens *within* a model's run (small's fills all share the skeleton prefix).
# Swap any name=path for name=mock to dry-run the control flow off-GPU.

:use big
> Write a Rust LRU cache: `pub struct Lru<K, V>` with `get(&mut self, k: &K) -> Option<&V>` and
> `put(&mut self, k: K, v: V)`. Give the full struct and impl, but leave each method body as `todo!()`.
:use small
:fill
:use big
> Here is the assembled cache. Review it for correctness and point out any eviction bug.
:check
:best
